    "basis": "OOT3D ZSI command 0x0F record stride 0x1c is now split into two promoted facts: command handler 0x00379188 stores the native list count/pointer at play+0x322c/+0x3230, and runtime consumer 0x0045dd50 reads that list through the environment state at play+0x3190 using current/previous/target/blend fields at play+0x3235/+0x3236/+0x3237/+0x3258. The renderer therefore uses the byte triplets that 0x0045dd50 copies directly: ambient RGB at record+0x0a, light0 signed direction at +0x0d, light0 RGB at +0x10, light1 signed direction at +0x13, light1 RGB at +0x16, and fog/environment RGB at +0x19. For CMB skeleton vertex lighting, native PICA uniforms confirm f82/f84/f81 are those resolved environment ambient/light0/light1 colors, while f80/f83 are the opposite compact actor vectors produced by 0x0045dd50 and consumed through 0x00253a4c/0x003130a4. The older first-15-byte EnvLightSettings-style prefix and actor-packet RGB candidate remain diagnostic data only. Native CMB materials, TextureEnv records, render-state fields, normals, skinning transforms, and PICA shadow route diagnostics remain preserved from extracted OOT3D assets/code.bin structures without N64 runtime asset substitution.",
