      "The final PICA light equation, channel routing and material combiner interaction still require trace-backed validation against OOT3D or an emulator PICA capture.",
      "The engine now preserves and diagnoses native CMB material raw texture-stage selectors, material header lighting flags, material colors/constants, render-state fields, MATS TextureEnvSetting records and decoded TextureEnv RGB programs; factorizable multi-stage previous/constant routes preserve primary-stage ColorScale and PICA clamp ordering in the backend shader, and supported additive constants are evaluated with PICA clamp semantics. CMB transform-instance and static baked vertex/hemisphere colors consume ambient/light0/light1 from the 0x0045dd50 resolved environment record, native material flags and normals; skeleton actors additionally consume the code.bin-derived compact actor vector packet. Link visual self-shadow/material shading is closed by that vertex/material path for the current fixture. The separate PICA Shadow2D route is explicit in the semantics table through LightEnv.shadow*, FragmentLightSource[].shadowed, Texture[0].shadowZ*, the Azahar PICA shadow selector equation, the Ohana PICA200 fragment-primary contribution equation and Shadow2D/ShadowCube sampling equation; native CMB skeleton materials are classified as Shadow2D-route candidates, but that projected shadow term remains unapplied until exact Shadow2D texture projection, encoded depth compare/filtering and backend render-state ordering are implemented. Full native implementation is still needed for true hemisphere lighting/occlusion channel routing, LUT/specular, attenuation and shadow projection/render-state ordering."
